# User avatar sizes

Back Office uses **three** round user-avatar sizes everywhere except the help guide FAB (that marketing asset is not a user avatar).

| Token | px | CSS variable | Use for |
|-------|-----|--------------|---------|
| **sm** | 22 | `--avatar-size-sm` | Dense rows: tables, timelines, multiselect options, pickers, chips |
| **med** | 28 | `--avatar-size-med` | Default: cards, comments, dropdown rows, TM field buttons |
| **lg** | 36 | `--avatar-size-lg` | Side panels, people lists, page title (`avatarOnly`), top-bar user menu, dialog member rows, upload dropzone thumb |

Source of truth: `admin/src/app/core/avatar-size.ts`, `:root` in `assets/layout/_core.scss`, and global classes in `assets/layout/_avatars.scss`.

## DOM classes (inspectable in devtools)

- **Round avatar element:** `ubo-avatar ubo-avatar--sm` | `ubo-avatar--med` | `ubo-avatar--lg`
- **Component host:** `ubo-avatar-size-sm` | `ubo-avatar-size-med` | `ubo-avatar-size-lg` on `app-person` and `app-tm-avatar`
- **Unassigned TM slot:** add `ubo-avatar--empty` with the size modifier classes

`app-person` / `app-tm-avatar` set these automatically from the `size` input. Static markup (top bar, @mention rows, Quill person cards, dropzone thumb, help chat bubbles) must include the same `ubo-avatar ubo-avatar--*` pair — do not size with inline `px` or lone CSS variables without the modifier class.

## Components

- **`app-person`** — CRM / activity / pipeline. `size="sm" | "med" | "lg"` (default `med`).
- **`app-tm-avatar`** — Task Manager and `app-people`. Same `size` input.

Do **not** pass pixel numbers to `size`. Do **not** add `xs`, `xl`, or ad-hoc `[size]="24"`.

## When CSS must set diameter (no component)

Prefer the **`ubo-avatar ubo-avatar--*`** classes. If a wrapper needs flex basis only, `flex: 0 0 var(--avatar-size-med)` is fine alongside those classes.

## Choosing a size

- Table or timeline row with name beside avatar → **sm**
- Standard inline person with label → **med**
- Side panel row, org people list, hero avatar on detail header → **lg**

If unsure, use **med**.

## Do not

- Hand-roll a fourth size in component `styles:` or page SCSS
- Use `p-avatar` for staff/contact photos (use `app-person` / `app-tm-avatar`)
- Size profile upload previews with `sm`/`med`/`lg` when the control is full-width `avatar-dropzone` `fill` / logo mode (those are upload UX, not list avatars)
- Rely on inline `width`/`height` in px instead of `ubo-avatar--*` classes
